{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating","id":1479868,"title":"How to get a higher Armor rating?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-30T22:46:52-07:00","id":1479868,"title":"How to get a higher Armor rating?","content":"Is there any way to improve on Mage Armor? Our ST is ruling That nothing stacks with Mage Armor, limiting us to 5 points of armor total. The adversaries he's throwing at us can dish out way more damage than that. Is he right, or is there a legal way to get a higher total armor rating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T00:47:38-07:00","id":1479872,"title":"","content":"The general rule of thumb of stacking in the CofD is that, unless a rule states specifically otherwise, you can stack as long as things come from different sources. You can't stack Mage Armors, or trying to give yourself armor directly with magic (like Life to transform your skin into something tough enough to qualify), because the source is the same. But you can stack Mage Armor and mundane armor and armor from a mundane Merit.<br /> <br /> It is your ST's prerogative on where the line is exactly, but you're definitely not supposed to be capped at armor 5 against physical attacks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T06:39:40-07:00","id":1479892,"title":"","content":"It's situationally limited by the nature of where you can use it, but the Amnion explicitly stacks with Armor from spells and Attainments, so your Dream Form, at least, can go over Armor 5 within the Astral with high enough Gnosis, highest-rated Subtle Arcanum, and Forces/Life/Matter.<br /> <br /> You can also use the Matter spell Aegis to raise the Armor rating of a physical piece of Armor above 5 by giving the spell enough Potency and spending a point of Mana, but that's not boosting Mage Armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T10:06:59-07:00","id":1479900,"title":"","content":"The Practice of Shielding might hold the answer you seek. A normal spell gives complete immunity from the natural and mundane phenomena being covered. Supernatural effects must win a Clash of Wills to even work.<br /> <br /> Which means that if, for example, a mage used a Shielding of Fate to gain protection from bullets and explosions, they could theoretically walk into a brutal shootout and be absolutely fine. But they wouldn't be as safe if the guns were magical. In addition, should enemies start punching, using melee weapons or should the buildings collapse on them, they wouldn't be covered.<br /> <br /> Mage Armor is great because it covers everything within its purview. But a mage could dedicate resources to additional defenses. Since mages know when Clashes of Will happen, they can add Willpower to the roll, on top of making sure to get a high modifier for a long lasting Shielding. A mage could in theory dedicate most of their spell control to become a resilient juggernaut and just use a magically boosted weapon, giving them a fearsome reputation of the practical warrior who no one seems to wound.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, bypass the problem entirely. Move to the phase of Twilight the enemy can't access and snipe them from it, or sneak away using it and Veiling spells. Scout ahead using familiars, scrying windows, astral projection, drones, cameras, animals (Life magic to see what an animal sees via Unveiling), all those can give opportunities for remote casting. They could also use Lying Maps or Warding so enemies can't even chase after the cabal. There are a ton of options, the greatest strength of mages is how flexible they can be when it comes to problemsolving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-01-2022, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T10:33:37-07:00","id":1479961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating?p=1479872#post1479872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is your ST's prerogative on where the line is exactly, but you're definitely not supposed to be capped at armor 5 against physical attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well at least not in the sense that there's any specifically stated cap at all. It's not as if getting an armour rating of even 5 is straightforward in any event. Options are powerful magic or going about in the bulkiest and most expensive equipment available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T11:59:11-07:00","id":1479967,"title":"","content":"If your conflicts as a mage are being predominantly decided by damage output and how much armor you're allowed to have, this probably isn't a normal Mage game. <br /> <br /> Can you provide more context on the setting you're playing in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T01:55:29-07:00","id":1484186,"title":"","content":"This strikes me as less a rules problem and more of an ST-player disconnect issue. I have never been in a pure mage game where armor 5 wasn't enough to survive several hits from a heavy-hitter. Maybe mixed games that built combat encounters for the werewolves. At the point you have an arcana at 5 to get the mage armor that high you probably have better options than damage based combat (Teleport to a volcano, yeet them into the atmosphere and shred them with friction, Turn them into a squirrel, temporal stasis, Prison realm and so on).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T11:48:59-07:00","id":1484228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating?p=1484186#post1484186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This strikes me as less a rules problem and more of an ST-player disconnect issue. I have never been in a pure mage game where armor 5 wasn't enough to survive several hits from a heavy-hitter. Maybe mixed games that built combat encounters for the werewolves. At the point you have an arcana at 5 to get the mage armor that high you probably have better options than damage based combat (Teleport to a volcano, yeet them into the atmosphere and shred them with friction, Turn them into a squirrel, temporal stasis, Prison realm and so on).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You would be suprised, it all depends on the tier of the antagonist. We were breaking down the combat power of a vampire in a recent thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484022#post1484022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With BP 5 you can have:<br /> <br /> 5 str + 5 vig + 5 skill + 5 BP frenzy + 8 for using 4 vitae for physical intensity and still remain 1 vitae to activate vigor.<br /> <br /> At BP 10, maximizing everything just for the sake of play who has it bigger, you can reach:<br /> <br /> Str 10 + skill 10 + Vigor 5 + 18 physical intensity (9 vitae) + 10 BP (frenzy) = 53. You can consider also Protean 5 to get another+5 on the grab roll = 58. And with Force of Nature you can move another 10-15 points to strength...<br /> <br /> Also, I think vampires have one of the most broken combat power: swarm form: you roll the whole pool - included disciplines - ignoring defense and armor and taking only 1 or 2 damages per attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if we consider that the vampire is not taking a turn to grow the Protean claws and is not going into frenzy, then they have the ability to spontaneously make attacks with a 47 dice pool, each of which do [weapon modifier]+5. Mage armor cannot cover that and even if they dodge using Acceleration with the rote bonus, its still incredibly dangerous. Should the mage survive the attack and considering that the vampire might target a limb (which is likely with such a huge dice pool), then it means its very possible that damage will overflow to aggravated, permanently tearing said limb off. They may also choose to use any size 10 object as an improvised or thrown weapon, which are objects the size of a sports car or a moose, easily securing the +5 lethal damage modifier.<br /> <br /> A max power vampire who is really angry can instead focus all their power into Physical Intensity to gain the ability, for a turn, to throw a dump truck, houseboat, tour bus or even a whale.<br /> <br /> Then if you consider they can spend a point of Vitae to reduce damage from all sources by 5 for that turn, even spells, means they can be terrifyingly durable. Plus with a blood pool of 75 and the ability to spend 10 per turn means a vampire with full resources can do this consistently for 6-7 turns. Keep in mind, we haven't accounted for any Devotions or fighting styles they may have, so lethality can still go up. Vampires are some of the most powerful physical combatants, werewolf teamwork is an incredible force multiplier and so on.<br /> <br /> A mage would probably be more successful by bypassing the problem entirely with clever spellwork. The Ancient One cannot beat Hulk by raw physical might, even Thor and Iron Man's Hulkbuster armor had a very tough time against him, but astrally projecting him secures her the win much more easily and cleanly than anyone else.<br /> <br /> If the players suspect a powerful enemy may try to sneak attack them and they are not confident on being able to detect or react to it fast enough, I can see why one may want a higher armor rating, even if its not the most efficient solution. But this is speculation for end game level power and, at that point, players should be acclimated to similar challenges, having resources, contingencies, equipment, allies and combat plans to be able to handle it. Even if its not reached that level, I imagine there would be some foreshadowing for players to deduce danger is on the way and have some leeway to prepare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-16-2022, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T15:44:52-07:00","id":1484240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating?p=1484228#post1484228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You would be suprised, it all depends on the tier of the antagonist. We were breaking down the combat power of a vampire in a recent thread:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So if we consider that the vampire is not taking a turn to grow the Protean claws and is not going into frenzy, then they have the ability to spontaneously make attacks with a 47 dice pool, each of which do [weapon modifier]+5. Mage armor cannot cover that and even if they dodge using Acceleration with the rote bonus, its still incredibly dangerous. Should the mage survive the attack and considering that the vampire might target a limb (which is likely with such a huge dice pool), then it means its very possible that damage will overflow to aggravated, permanently tearing said limb off. They may also choose to use any size 10 object as an improvised or thrown weapon, which are objects the size of a sports car or a moose, easily securing the +5 lethal damage modifier.<br /> <br /> A max power vampire who is really angry can instead focus all their power into Physical Intensity to gain the ability to throw a yacht, light airplane or semi truck for a turn.<br /> <br /> Then if you consider they can spend a point of Vitae to reduce damage from all sources by 5 for that turn, even spells, means they can be terrifyingly durable. Plus with a blood pool of 75 and the ability to spend 10 per turn means a vampire with full resources can do this consistently for 6-7 turns. Keep in mind, we haven't accounted for any Devotions or fighting styles they may have, so lethality can still go up. Vampires are some of the most powerful physical combatants, werewolf teamwork is an incredible force multiplier and so on. <br /> <br /> A mage would probably be more successful by bypassing the problem entirely with clever spellwork. The Ancient One cannot beat Hulk by raw physical might, even Thor and Iron Man's Hulkbuster armor had a very tough time against him, but astrally projecting him secures her the win much more easily and cleanly than anyone else.<br /> <br /> If the players suspect a powerful enemy may try to sneak attack them and they are not confident on being able to detect or react to it fast enough, I can see why one may want a higher armor rating, even if its not the most efficient solution. But this is speculation for end game level power and, at that point, players should be acclimated to similar challenges, having resources, contingencies, equipment, allies and combat plans to be able to handle it. Even if its not reached that level, I imagine there would be some foreshadowing for players to deduce danger is on the way and have some leeway to prepare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just few minor correction:<br /> <br /> 1. Protean 2+4 is reflexive, so no action is required<br /> 2. Resilience 5 absorb 6 damages of any source (also aggravated) which are no bane. And just 5 from Bane's source.<br /> 3. When you can make aggravated damages it's not worth to throw huge objects. I honestly think that the mechanics for such kind of attacks is poorly designed and underdeveloped, but if we have to go by book it's rarely worth of (if not to force opponent for a full defensive turn -admitting that a car is to big to be avoided with only defense. I would rather require at least a dodge action)<br /> 4. I would rather go for a grab because: it prevent any opponent attack until the vampire can mantain the control; if he has unnatural affinity can drink vitae while damaging at full pool to continue boosting attributes to mantain the grab (possibly also healing any injury)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T22:59:25-07:00","id":1484267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating?p=1484240#post1484240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. I would rather go for a grab because: it prevent any opponent attack until the vampire can mantain the control; if he has unnatural affinity can drink vitae while damaging at full pool to continue boosting attributes to mantain the grab (possibly also healing any injury)</div> </div> </div> </div>At BP 5 the vampire doesn't need Unnatural Affinity to be able to gain Vitae from a mage (or any of the other living splats).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T23:21:03-07:00","id":1484268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating?p=1484267#post1484267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At BP 5 the vampire doesn't need Unnatural Affinity to be able to gain Vitae from a mage (or any of the other living splats).</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I didn't know actually. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T01:54:58-07:00","id":1484273,"title":"","content":"If you are dealing with a vampire, why are you trying to fight it physically? Yeet it in space, teleport it to the other side of the world where it is noon or just grow a miniature sun into their head, why going physical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T02:03:23-07:00","id":1484274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating?p=1484273#post1484273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeet it in space, teleport it to the other side of the world where it is noon or just grow a miniature sun into their head, why going physical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you don't have Space 4 or Forces 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T03:04:35-07:00","id":1484278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating?p=1484273#post1484273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are dealing with a vampire, why are you trying to fight it physically? Yeet it in space, teleport it to the other side of the world where it is noon or just grow a miniature sun into their head, why going physical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Serious answers<br /> <br /> <b>Yeet it into space</b>: If we are talking &quot;past the stratosphere&quot;, with normal sensory range, this may actually be quite difficult, especially during the night. If we are talking sympathetic range, few mages are going to have a sympathy Yantra for &quot;outer space&quot; at hand in a flash or indeed the sympathy for it to begin with. If we are just talking &quot;really high up&quot;, then the flat 10 lethal damage from a terminal velocity fall is actually quite survivable for the undead, especially if Resilience is involved (though in that case the real advantage is the Turns of other actions you buy yourself while they fall). Besides help from Resilience, Animalism and Protean can save the vampire from fall damage entirely. Perhaps even Celerity can interact with fall damage, depending on how the ST rationalizes what Celerity does. Depending on the environment, Vigor may also be useful in breaking the fall.<br /> <br /> <b>teleport it to the other side of the world where it is noon &amp; miniature sun: </b>Very dependent on the Blood Potency and Humanity of the target vampire. In the worst cases (for others) you just unleashed a rampaging monster on some unsuspecting Sleepers on the other side of the world (with the likely hit to Wisdom that comes with it) or you barely dealt any damage to them. The likely fear frenzy does help you but could also be turned into Riding the Wave against you.<br /> There is also the non-zero chance of them being a Master of the Mystery of the Ascendant or having some other tricks that interact with sunlight damage.<br /> &quot;Inside their head&quot; is a bit iffy I feel without other Arcana besides Forces 5 being involved. You are not targeting their Pattern (any of them), you are Making something inside their body, which should generally be concealed from your sensory range. A Death Unveiling may be enough to see &quot;through&quot; the undead enough for this to work though. Of course the Path most likely to have Forces 5 is the least likely to have Death 1.<br /> <br /> None of these are inherently bad ideas, but they are either more difficult or less reliable than you present. This should be taken as exemplary for most &quot;100% Vampire Removal Spells [Elders hate it!]&quot;. In the end, we have the old dilemma of white rooms being mostly useless in a game with characters so asymmetric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T03:43:16-07:00","id":1484279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating?p=1484278#post1484278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serious answers<br /> <br /> <b>Yeet it into space</b>: If we are talking &amp;quot;past the stratosphere&amp;quot;, with normal sensory range, this may actually be quite difficult, especially during the night. If we are talking sympathetic range, few mages are going to have a sympathy Yantra for &amp;quot;outer space&amp;quot; at hand in a flash or indeed the sympathy for it to begin with. If we are just talking &amp;quot;really high up&amp;quot;, then the flat 10 lethal damage from a terminal velocity fall is actually quite survivable for the undead, especially if Resilience is involved (though in that case the real advantage is the Turns of other actions you buy yourself while they fall). Besides help from Resilience, Animalism and Protean can save the vampire from fall damage entirely. Perhaps even Celerity can interact with fall damage, depending on how the ST rationalizes what Celerity does. Depending on the environment, Vigor may also be useful in breaking the fall.<br /> <br /> <b>teleport it to the other side of the world where it is noon &amp; miniature sun: </b>Very dependent on the Blood Potency and Humanity of the target vampire. In the worst cases (for others) you just unleashed a rampaging monster on some unsuspecting Sleepers on the other side of the world (with the likely hit to Wisdom that comes with it) or you barely dealt any damage to them. The likely fear frenzy does help you but could also be turned into Riding the Wave against you.<br /> There is also the non-zero chance of them being a Master of the Mystery of the Ascendant or having some other tricks that interact with sunlight damage.<br /> &amp;quot;Inside their head&amp;quot; is a bit iffy I feel without other Arcana besides Forces 5 being involved. You are not targeting their Pattern (any of them), you are Making something inside their body, which should generally be concealed from your sensory range. A Death Unveiling may be enough to see &amp;quot;through&amp;quot; the undead enough for this to work though. Of course the Path most likely to have Forces 5 is the least likely to have Death 1.<br /> <br /> None of these are inherently bad ideas, but they are either more difficult or less reliable than you present. This should be taken as exemplary for most &amp;quot;100% Vampire Removal Spells [Elders hate it!]&amp;quot;. In the end, we have the old dilemma of white rooms being mostly useless in a game with characters so asymmetric.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree with you. Also, even just protean 1 is suficient to rest safe until night if teleported on the other side of the world at noon.<br /> <br /> Also, there's always the uncertainity of who act first due to celerity. I think the Clash of Wills would decide the outcome of the encounter as such physical vampire is pretty much able to subdue the mage (or even kill him with such a pool) in the very first turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T03:58:37-07:00","id":1484280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating?p=1484279#post1484279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I generally agree with you. Also, even just protean 1 is suficient to rest safe until night if teleported on the other side of the world at noon.<br /> <br /> Also, there's always the uncertainity of who act first due to celerity. I think the Clash of Wills would decide the outcome of the encounter as such physical vampire is pretty much able to subdue the mage (or even kill him with such a pool) in the very first turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if we assume that the vampire automatically goes first because the mage has no Time, there are multiple ways how various Arcana could either make the Awakened effectively untouchable or at least capable of surviving a full Vitae force assault from a comparable vampire. But will the mage actually have those spells up when the fight starts? Is she perhaps laboring under crippling Paradox Conditions as a result of those (or other) castings? Will the vampire have some Devotion, Coil or Ritual effect that makes the mage less untouchable than she thought? That's something a white room just can't decide.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T04:01:45-07:00","id":1484281,"title":"","content":"Yes, I agree!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T05:30:11-07:00","id":1484285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating?p=1484273#post1484273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are dealing with a vampire, why are you trying to fight it physically? Yeet it in space, teleport it to the other side of the world where it is noon or just grow a miniature sun into their head, why going physical?</div> </div> </div> </div>More important than all the more nuanced considerations of why a White Room isn't that useful is...<br /> <br /> The thread isn't about how to deal with a Vampire. This isn't an intrinsically easy or hard thing and vampires would have the same general consideration for Mages.<br /> <br /> What the thread questions is how to deal with it <b><u><i>specifically</i></u></b> through Armor. So a physical confrontation is the very premise of the question.<br /> <br /> On that regard, Armor 5 definitely isn't enough by itself to survive actual supernatural heavy hitters. And Mages have ways to get more, but aren't meant to easily stack huge Armor values. And that isn't necessarily a bad thing, because what the Mage has against other supernaturals is exactly the ability to more easily <i>remove the physical confrontation from the equation</i>. If they can't do that in a high-end scenario, being able to brace ludicrous damage with Armor alone would be to drop the themes and concept to just make them ignore the strengths of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T08:22:10-07:00","id":1484288,"title":"","content":"In that case, I think the <i>Aegis</i> spell (core book page 156) would be the simplest option. I believe the effect could also be accomplished with a Perfecting of Fate. Using Perfecting spells to increase Wits, Dexterity and Athletics automatically increases defense as well, which is not specifically armor but can make a tangible difference. When focused on dodging, use of <i>Acceleration </i>with rote quality (core book page 188) creates another very powerful way to avoid deadly attacks, creating a chance to reposition for a counterattack, distract a foe while cabalmates prepare something powerful or even escape the battle altogether.<br /> <br /> Following in the spirit of creating a powerful magical armor, in theory you could possibly use a combination of Fate and Space to build upon the <i>Ban</i> spell (core book page 176), which would only exclude things that done with hostile intent. It wouldn't cover automatons, natural occurrences, sensory spells or ones cast at sympathetic range. However, most threats would just pass through the mage, unless they use a supernatural power that can enter and win a Clash of Wills, making it a very potent defense nonetheless. Alternatively, there is a way to create <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1473459#post1473459\"> a version of this with Time</a>. That could create invulnerability against anything that doesn't win a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> Lastly, there is always the option of using magic to design and build top quality armor (<i>Shaping</i> and <i>Enhance Skill</i> are some examples of these spells), obtaining a high modifier (+5 in general and/or ballistic armor) which spells can build upon to higher levels that stack with mage armor. This would probably require expensive components, which can be mitigated by perfected materials (such as perfected leather blocking all bashing damage). However, chances are you will also need to use Veiling spells to disguise the equipment.<br /> <br /> But as far as stacking goes, I would say Mage Armor should only stack against things the armor defends against. Prime armor will not work against bullets, Spirit armor will not help against aimed spells, Mind armor offers nothing against automatons and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-18-2022, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T03:07:15-07:00","id":1484854,"title":"","content":"So unless you want to go all-in on Aegis (which is the only way I can think of to gain Armor 6+), then trying to confront a &quot;Maxed out Vampire&quot; on a purely physical manner is a bad idea. Vampires will do that better than a mage. So will werewolves. Ray physical challenges in a white room environment is, in fact a weakness of most mages. Side note: for this example you seem to be giving it all disciplines at 5, blood potency 10, skill and attribute 10 but not giving the mage dots in any specific arcana, seems a bit skewed to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T06:21:46-07:00","id":1484862,"title":"","content":"Actually, I am assuming a max stat, Gnosis 10, all Arcana you need at 5 mage. Such a mage can defeat the vampire in melee, but it will be suboptimal.<br /> <br /> So lets say the vampire started combat suddenly, the mage can use the reflexive version of Exceptional Luck to gain Charmed, in addition to a mage armor of your choice. This is because we are facing a max vampire, so there is no way to get enough Potency to overcome his Withstand and apply Knocked Down via a hex, at least not without previous preparations. The exception would be if the mage had personally made Exceptional Luck into a rote, granting them a higher chance at getting an exceptional success to bypass Withstand. A vampire playing things safe would start with a grapple, relying on his Disciplines to get an exceptional success and only then attack for massive damage, which Charmed still covers.<br /> <br /> The next move is Temporal Pocket boosted by Time in a Bottle. Now you have a year's worth of time to prepare your next move (you might also want Veil of Moments to survive without food). If the vampire grappled you, then you Teleport out.<br /> <br /> This is the turning point, from here you secure victory. The optimal move is to use Miracle to give an exceptional success on an Unmaking spell, completely bypassing Withstand and one shotting the vampire (like using one of Forces for a classic disintegration beam) or a sleeping spell if you are going the high Wisdom route. Using this path, you will burn through some mana, but not much.<br /> <br /> The suboptimal way is to use cast buffs to all your Physical Attributes using Life, spending mana on boosting them beyond trait limits, surpassing Vigor's bonus. Then cast Acceleration to overcome Celerity. Now add a high Potency healing time boosting spell to make you more resilient than a werewolf. Now cast Endurance of the Ages to protect you from any vampires attacks, unless they win a Clash of Wills. Next is boosting your equipment as much as you can using Matter, giving max damage per hit. Lastly, boost your Willpower dice bonus via Mind for a safety measure in Clashes of Wills, alongside mental Attributes (Wits is especially important for defense) and any relevant skills (your main weapon skill and Athletics for even more defense). With all that, you stand a chance of defeating them in melee combat, but they can still kill you in one good hit.<br /> <br /> You can do all this using normal preparation time instead of Temporal Pocket, but I also wanted to illustrate the worst case scenario. The first option would use some mana and secure a win with minimal risk, with preparation time you can do it at sympathetic range for no risk at all. The second option uses a lot more mana, commits more spell control and is still placing you within one shot range. High defense makes you difficult to hit, high general armor absorbs a lot of damage, plus high HP and high speed regeneration makes you very durable. But the vampire can still hit for a scary amount, then again so can you and Exceptional Luck gives Charmed as a safety net.<br /> <br /> There are more things that can be done, but I think the general idea comes across, a pure melee win is doable, but resource intensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-24-2022, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T08:37:15-07:00","id":1484969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479868-how-to-get-a-higher-armor-rating#post1479868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to improve on Mage Armor? Our ST is ruling That nothing stacks with Mage Armor, limiting us to 5 points of armor total. The adversaries he's throwing at us can dish out way more damage than that. Is he right, or is there a legal way to get a higher total armor rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use Shielding spells and/or give yourself general armor rating with Creative Thaumaturgy spells. With Advanced Duration/Scale you can target whole cabal and make it stick for some time, while putting all your dice into Potency would result in having 6+ armor ratings. Use magic to buff your magic for this spell; Exceptional Luck, As Above So Below, Choose the Thread are all good for those purposes. Don't forget that you can create Steadfast (Your Magic), reduce casting pool to 1 with penalties and still be guaranteed success on the spell. Ritual spellcasting, spending willpower and doing teamwork helps as well. With all this, Potency 10 spells are hard, but not impossible.<br /> <br /> Also, don't forget that since armor rating can have different stacking sources (for example, you can wear body armor while having magic force shield on yourself), different <i>magical</i> sources of armor may stack as well; for example, personally I would've allowed to stack armor given by Aegis, and, say, Forces-analogue of Aegis. Your ST may disagree, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}